## PHASE 3 — SAFETY CONSTRAINTS (NON-NEGOTIABLE)

If any of these would be violated, STOP and report before proceeding:

❌ DO NOT modify any N1 class touching DB, Kafka, messaging, or event publishing
❌ DO NOT modify any N1 class outside the codebase hardgate execution path
❌ DO NOT copy C1 dependencies that pull in its DB/Kafka/broker clients
❌ DO NOT change method signatures of any existing N1 public API
❌ DO NOT delete or rename any existing N1 hardgate class
✅ All new classes go in: [n1.base.package].integration.c1
✅ C1 logic called via adapter only — no direct static calls
✅ If C1 throws ANY exception: catch in adapter, log with full context,
auto-fallback to N1 legacy logic — exception must never propagate upward

